Waterloo MCP server

This package exposes read-only access to Waterloo data roots over MCP.

Current v1 focus:
- list configured roots
- inspect the indexed Waterloo data behind them
- keep the server simple and stdio-based for local development
- offer Streamable HTTP for Inspector-based inspection at `/mcp`

The current entry point is `wtrl_mcp`.
The Inspector-friendly entry point is `sdv.doc.waterloo.mcp.server:app`.

Typical usage:
- use `--config` to select a TOML file explicitly
- or keep `wtrl_mcp.toml` next to `server.py` as the default configuration
- use `--gen-config-template` to print a template to stdout
- configure `transport = "stdio"` or `transport = "streamable-http"` in the
  TOML file
- browser Inspector example:
  - set `transport = "streamable-http"` in the TOML file
  - set `allowed_origins = ["http://gilgamesh:6274"]`
  - set `allowed_hosts = ["127.0.0.1:8000"]`
  - connect the Inspector to `http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp`
- inspect `tools/list`
- call `list_docs`

The server is intentionally read-only in v1.
